{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310517,"nonce":"J+mH8qRVPeXhNUxryKPx5/O50yg=","title":"SCOPE — abstract operator overloading capability matrix; `String == Slice` blocked by 2 compiler bugs (abstract-over-class/struct field ...","message":"**Scoped 2026-07 for user's ask \"compare String to Slice via operator overloading.\"** Verdict: NOT a stdlib change — needs 2 compiler fixes. **DEFERRED as a follow-up per user** (cost=implement abstract-over-non-primitive, a regression-risky compiler feature; payoff=`==` sugar over already-working `.equalsString()`). Pick up deliberately if abstract-over-class is wanted as a general capability. No code changed.\n\n**Capability matrix (empirical, current binary — tests in /tmp/optest):**\n- `@:op(A+B)` on abstract-over-**Int** → Haxe method: ✅ (T3 `3+4=7`).\n- `@:op(A==B)` abstract-vs-**String**, abstract on **LEFT** (`x == \"s\"`): ✅ (T4a). Asymmetric-RHS-type already works.\n- `@:commutative` (String on LEFT, `\"s\" == x`): ❌ returns false — ignored (T4b).\n- abstract-over-**class** (`abstract T(TagImpl)`): construction/dispatch/`return this` ✅ but **field access `this.field` HANGS** (T2/T6/H2). Spins in downstream string concat (garbage String ptr).\n- abstract-over-**anon-struct**: field read → **garbage** (T5, `hi/7`→`empty/0`), same root.\n\n**Fix #1 — abstract-over-class/struct is UNIMPLEMENTED, not a one-line patch. MIR-CONFIRMED (RAYZOR_DUMP_MIR, /tmp/optest).** The abstract is represented as a **primitive (i32), NOT a pointer to its class underlying** → three simultaneous breakages: (1) return-type truncation — `@of(...) -\u003e i32` truncates the 64-bit TagImpl ptr; (2) wrong field GEP — `@num` emits `gep i32 $0,[2]` = byte 8, but 2nd field is at byte 16 (GEP multiplies field-INDEX by the field's own type size, not the struct slot size); (3) non-identity ctor value-wrap — `new Tag(s){this=new TagImpl(s)}` collapses to the raw arg (hir_to_mir.rs:19020-19028 returns args[0] for any single-arg abstract new without a user CLASS ctor). Primitive-underlying abstracts (Int64/UInt/SIMD/Meters) work because i32/i64 repr is correct for them. Fix = give class/struct-underlying abstracts a pointer repr + correct field layout + real ctor execution, without regressing primitive ones — a proper feature implementation across the abstract→IR-type map, field-GEP, and abstract-new lowering. Effort: SIGNIFICANT (not the \"moderate\" first-guess). The earlier \"this by-value param0\" (tast_to_hir.rs:3254) is a symptom, not the whole cause.\n\n**Fix #2 — @:commutative + RHS-type operator resolution. MODERATE (additive, lower risk).** ROOT: binary-op rewrite resolves the @:op method from the **LHS owner only**, matched by operator DISCRIMINANT (not RHS type), no commutative path (tast_to_hir.rs ~4560-4616 + caller). `@:commutative` never parsed anywhere in parser/compiler. `String == abstract` → LHS String has no @:op → no rewrite → default `==` → false. Fix: (a) detect `@:commutative` meta on the @:op method; (b) when LHS yields no op, check RHS operand's abstract for a matching commutative @:op and emit call with operands swapped; (c) overload-match @:op(A==B) by the OTHER operand's type so `==String` vs `==Slice` disambiguate.\n\n**Together** → full `String == Slice` both directions; then [[project_slice_zero_copy_string_view]] becomes `abstract Slice(SliceImpl)` with `@:op(A==B)(String)` + `@:commutative`. **Smaller path:** if only `slice == \"str\"` (abstract-left) is wanted, Fix #1 alone suffices (asymmetric already works); `\"str\" == slice` needs Fix #2 too. Combined ~1 focused session, Fix #1 paces it. NOTE: operator resolution is per-current-file (find_operator_method reads current_typed_file) — x-module abstract operators may need the by-name index too.\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `bugs_abstract_operator_overloading_scope` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}